  "result": "Perfect! All 166 tests pass. I've successfully added payment tracking:\n\n**src/payments.js** - Two functions:\n\n1. **recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })** - Records a payment:\n   - Validates invoice status is 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (NOT_ISSUED error otherwise)\n   - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID for zero, negative, or fractional)\n   - Validates date is in YYYY-MM-DD format (DATE_INVALID error)\n   - Checks payment doesn't exceed balance due (OVERPAYMENT error)\n   - Creates payments array if missing\n   - Appends payment with amount and date\n   - Auto-updates status:\n     - 'paid' when balance becomes zero\n     - 'partially_paid' when balance remains\n   - Never mutates input invoice\n\n2. **balanceDue(invoice)** - Calculates amount owed:\n   - Uses invoiceTotals to get invoice total\n   - Sums all payments\n   - Returns total - paid (clamped at 0)\n\n**src/errors.js** - Added two error codes:\n- `NOT_ISSUED`: Payments only allowed on issued or partially_paid invoices\n- `OVERPAYMENT`: Payment exceeds what's owed\n\n**Tests** - 16 new tests covering:\n- Creating payments array on first payment\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Rejecting draft and fully paid invoices\n- Amount validation (zero, negative, non-integer)\n- Overpayment detection\n- Date validation\n- Multiple sequential payments\n- Input immutability\n- Balance due with no payments, partial, full, and multiple payments\n\nThe implementation enables full payment tracking with automatic status management based on the remaining balance due.",
